          "quote": "(field (name \"Description\") \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"219\") (name \"VOUTN\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"220\") (name \"VOUTP\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed MPN is sourced, a 24Ω resistor will load VOUTP–VOUTN instead of providing the intended 24kΩ path, potentially causing excessive current and disrupting or damaging that output circuit.",
      "confidence": 0.96
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U15", "U22", "U35", "U36"],
      "pins": ["U15.1", "U15.4", "U22.1", "U22.4", "U35.1", "U35.4", "U36.1", "U36.4"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_SINK1", "ESTOP_SINK2", "ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL", "Net-(U15-Y)", "/ESTOP_SINK_ALL", "ESTOP_OUT"],
      "observed": "The e-stop buffers are valued SN74LVC1G07, but their listed MPN is U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R. A 1G125 is a tri-state push-pull buffer, not the open-drain buffer indicated by the 1G07 value and intended sink function.",
      "expected": "The e-stop sink stages should use the specified open-drain buffer type, or another component that preserves the intended sink-only behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "`U15`, `U22`, `U35`, `U36` (`SN74LVC1G07`) wired as `/OE` gates on `ESTOP_SINK1`/`ESTOP_SINK2`/`ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL`"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U15\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(property (name \"MPN\") (value \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U15\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"/OE\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U36\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Y\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed 1G125 parts are fitted, enabled stages can actively drive their outputs high as well as low, rather than behaving as open-drain sinks. That can alter or interfere with the intended e-stop sink-loop behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show a clear resistor sourcing mismatch: R36 is specified as 24kΩ but its listed part is 24Ω. They also list push-pull 1G125 parts for the e-stop stages specified as open-drain 1G07 sink buffers, which could change the safety-loop behavior."
}

